<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Human evolution</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as anthropogeny, anthropogenesis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Human evolution is the evolutionary history of Homo sapiens, a species of the hominid family of primates, studied through physical and evolutionary anthropology, paleontology and genetics. Primates diverged from other mammals about 85 million years ago, and the extinct biped ancestors of humans separated from the genus Pan, which includes chimpanzees and bonobos, 4–7 million years ago. The genus Homo is evidenced by the appearance of H. habilis, and anatomically modern humans emerged in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> approximately 300,000 years ago. Over this history humans developed bipedalism, dexterity and complex language, and modern humans interbred with archaic humans such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neanderthal">Neanderthals</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denisovan">Denisovans</a>.</p></div>
